===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sek-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|risqué|t=risky}}, an {{glossary|adjective}} use of the {{glossary|past}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|fr|risquer|t=to put at risk; to risk}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=6152196486|date=December 2024}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=adj}}</ref> from {{m|fr|risque|t=risk|pos=n}} + {{m|fr|-er|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|infinitive}}s of first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|verb}}s}}. {{m|fr||Risque}} is derived from {{der|en|roa-oit|risco|t=risk}} (modern {{cog|it|rischio}}), possibly a {{glossary|deverbal}} from {{m|roa-oit|resecare}} or from {{der|en|VL.|*resecum}}, both from {{der|en|la|resecō|t=to cut loose or off, etc.}}, from {{m|la|re-|pos={{glossary|intensifying}} {{glossary|prefix}}}} + {{m|la|secō|t=to cut; to cut off}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sek-|t=to cut; to cut off, sever}}).

